import json,csv,hashlib
from pathlib import Path
b=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;queue=list(csv.DictReader((b/'queue.csv').open()));g=json.loads((b/'lead-gaia-covariance.json').read_text());cl=json.loads((b/'lead-clocks.json').read_text())
texts={
'408996985':('confirmed','target-supported','new-eligible','Three separate observing occasions show matching abrupt long, flat-bottomed eclipses: S59 BTJD2930.82703, S73 3288.71344, S86 3646.53842, depths24.8–27.1ppt, duration2.11–2.16d. Fitted clock59.6426155d using cycles0/6/12, conditional formal error0.00118d; scatter about0.0205d requires allowance beyond the formal fit. Raw coverage rejects divisors3–6, but half-period29.8213d and other sparse integer alternatives survive coverage. Gaia59.58441±0.05740d resolves the unique nearby orbital period; period assignment is Gaia-assisted. Its edge-on conjunction offsets1.78–2.48d fall within source covariance2.30–2.98d; nonlinear covariance also evaluated with nominal-branch unwrapping. Custom TESScut3x3 recovers25ppt loss and deficit0.234pixel from target. Nearby G15.42 source15.6arcsec north is capable by brightness alone; deficit lies toward/below target, not toward that neighbor. Pixel localization plus Gaia coherence support target, subject to unresolved companions.','More observing coverage can independently resolve photometric half-period alias and refine long-event timings.'),
'455100744':('confirmed','target-supported','new-eligible','S61 primary BTJD2972.87141 has71.4ppt depth and0.549d duration. Distinct shallower conjunction at2985.67612 repeats S88 at3697.93504,13.7–14.2ppt and0.428–0.439d. Same-kind secondary clock44.5161826d across16cycles, conditional formal error0.000884d with0.01d epoch floor. Raw covered divisors2–6 have clean nulls; sparse integer7/8/9/10 alternatives remain but are incompatible with Gaia44.53754±0.04428d. The period is Gaia-assisted, not a blind unique photometric ephemeris. Both eclipse kinds are distinct and not counted as same-kind repeats. Covariance geometry accommodates primary and secondary offsets; MC branches unwrapped before fixed-cycle propagation. Custom aperture recovers67ppt primary, centered difference0.059pixel on isolated bright target.','A further secondary or primary occasion would refine period independently of Gaia.'),
'467460090':('plausible','source-hold-known-capable-EB','source-hold','Raw QLP shows many near-total short-period eclipses across seven sectors; repeated signal is real in extracted photometry but grossly inconsistent with the29.30476d Gaia orbit. Neighbor IJspeert EB TIC467459980 lies44.15arcsec away; VSX GL Car EA+HB lies35.90arcsec away. No neighboring identity is substituted for the queued target. The representative custom cutout numeric offset1.38pixel is displaced; initial rendering failed on a blank neighbor magnitude and needs audit. Large geometry covariance cannot establish that the short eclipses belong to the29d SB1. Target physical classification remains plausible/source-hold despite real eclipses in the field.','Resolve source with pixel model/neighbor ephemeris; do not count target or neighbor as new addition.'),
'467864145':('confirmed','target-supported','new-eligible','S60 has two unequal flat-bottomed eclipses at2941.54737 and2959.77252,29.0 and15.2ppt with~1.8d widths. S73 shows partial repeats of both kinds. Free fits to partial events are explicitly unusable. Fixed S60 morphology templates give A2941.54582?3306.07819 over10cycles,36.4532368d; B2959.77740?3287.85463 over9cycles,36.4530255d. ±5%template width changes each partial midpoint~0.04d, so0.005d is a conservative period allowance, not formal/calibrated uncertainty. Both opposite minima repeat separately; half-period18.2266d mixes unequal kinds. Covered divisors3–6 are refuted; other sparse integers require Gaia36.45333±0.01658d to choose the orbit. Covariance conjunction offsets+0.098/-0.063d are small relative to~1d errors. Custom aperture recovers23ppt, difference centroid0.032pixel on target; a G13.12 neighbor14.65arcsec north does not coincide with deficit.','Obtain full ingress on another event to replace template-dependent partial timing.'),
'15994632':('plausible','unresolved','no-prior-exact-EB','One narrow S75 event BTJD3361.44093 has21.5ppt fitted depth and0.078d duration on structured variability. No same-kind repeat is established in six raw sectors; no precise period is measured. Nearest Gaia conjunction offset-7.99d versus linear sigma1.665d contradicts assignment to selected orbit. Custom aperture sees a weaker~7ppt excursion and blended difference centroid1.12pixel from target near bright source; attribution unresolved. Nearby VSX SR and ROT entries are not prior exact target eclipsing classifications. Current sector inventory checked.','Find unflagged recurrent event and resolve bright-neighbor contamination before assigning physical target EB.'),
'132999153':('plausible','unresolved-flagged-pixels','no-prior-exact-EB','S54 narrow event BTJD2792.21682 fitted21.9ppt and0.070d; S81 does not establish recurrence. The initial screen flag was below contrast threshold, retained by visual morphology. QLP QUALITY0 does not override TESScut QUALITY2048 throughout the event: no usable q0 core exists. Missing/flagged pixels are unknown, not a null or an independent detection. KSPSAP same photons reproduces raw SAP excursion and supplies only reduction robustness. Gaia conjunction offset+6.11d with sigma2.75d is not decisive confirmation; no target period measured.','Acquire unflagged independent occasion and pixel attribution.'),
'257464332':('plausible','artifact-dominated-unresolved','no-prior-exact-EB','S94 shows a narrow deficit at3856.8556 at sector onset with missing earlier shoulder, plus broad~3874.92 variability. Similar discontinuities follow gaps and sector starts in later sectors. The free narrow fit17.5ppt/0.32d is phenomenological and does not establish an eclipse midpoint; the broad2.42d fit is structured variability, not a same-kind timing point. Custom3x3 aperture has no matching narrow loss in q0 data and an invalid zero-positive-weight centroid (NaN), so no localization claim is made. Gaia nearest offsets+12.31d narrow/-7.29d broad strongly disagree with source covariance~1.6d. Catalogue absence does not turn instrumental morphology into an EB.','Reinspect an unflagged event with complete shoulders and target pixel model; current target remains excluded.'),
'296080348':('plausible','artifact-suspect-flagged-pixels','no-prior-exact-EB','S80 has narrow fitted24.6ppt/0.050d excursion at3488.96522 on first postgap samples, with missing earlier shoulder and broad gap-associated changes in other sectors. All TESScut core cadences carry QUALITY2048 although QLP mask is0; no q0 attribution is available. This is a flagged window, not a clean astrophysical null. No second independent observing occasion establishes recurrence. Nearest Gaia conjunction offset-5.34d versus3.18d covariance does not confirm a common orbit.','Repeat under clean observing conditions and recover complete ingress/egress and attribution.')}
rows=[]
for r in queue:
 tic=r['tic'];verdict,source,novelty,body,nextcheck=texts[tic];dest=b/tic
 header=f"# {r['sample_id']} — TIC {tic}\n\nGaia DR3 {r['gaia_dr3']}; G={r['gaia_G']}; selection orbit P={r['gaia_period']}d. Exact queued identity retained.\n\nReview completion: completed bounded lead review; helper audit pending. Physical outcome: **{verdict}**. Source attribution: {source}. Novelty: {novelty}.\n\n"
 protocol='\n\nEvidence uses representative available raw QLP SAP events, q=0 and positive finite flux. Timing trapezoids are phenomenological, with correlated variability and missing shoulders noted above. Alternative custom TESScut apertures share TESS photons and test reduction/source robustness, never independent occasions. Gaia geometry uses source-specific full correlation submatrix and edge-on conjunctions; Monte Carlo draws unwrap to the nominal conjunction branch before fixed-cycle propagation. Successful shared catalogue queries cover Methods§2.7 source groups; source-specific known neighbors are retained, failed requests are never negative matches. Literature priority is scoped, not exhaustive.\n\nReceipts: lead-context.json, lead-series.json, lead-timing.json, lead-reduction.json, lead-neighbors.json, lead-central-catalogue-receipts.json, lead-localization-*.json where available. Batch-level lead-source-hashes.json and lead-raw-identity.json verify raw TIC headers and bytes. Scripts retained alongside queue.\n\nNext check: '+nextcheck+'\n'
 (dest/'REPORT.md').write_text(header+body+protocol,encoding='utf8')
 rows.append(dict(sample_id=r['sample_id'],tic=tic,gaia_dr3=r['gaia_dr3'],gaia_G=r['gaia_G'],gaia_period_d=r['gaia_period'],completion='lead-complete-helper-pending',physical_verdict=verdict,source_attribution=source,novelty=novelty,accepted_unique_addition=str(verdict=='confirmed').lower(),period_d=cl.get(tic,{}).get('period_d',''),period_error_d=cl.get(tic,{}).get('formal_period_error_d',''),period_error_meaning='conditional formal' if tic in ('408996985','455100744') else 'template sensitivity allowance' if tic=='467864145' else '',report=f'{tic}/REPORT.md',limitations=nextcheck))
with (b/'RESULTS.csv').open('w',newline='',encoding='utf8') as f:w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=rows[0]);w.writeheader();w.writerows(rows)
